verdict: "Above the waterline the citadel shows a sloped deck (70.1 deg from vertical on 60% of it); 16.3% of the side face is above the waterline and the roof is 2.1 m above the waterline. At broadside with flat fire, 60% of hits over the citadel strike its plate past 60 deg (effective thickness over double) and 60% at or past the shell's always-ricochet angle. At 12.0 km, 65.8% of hits over the citadel strike its plate past 60 deg (effective thickness over double) and 65.8% at or past the shell's always-ricochet angle."
assumptions:
  - "The waterline is model height 0, where the armor viewer draws the water."
  - "Rays are parallel and evenly spaced, so shares are by area seen along the ray direction."
  - "Effective thickness is thickness / cos(strike angle) with no normalization. Shell events use the shell's normalization for the fuse and its ricochet angles; ricochets between the two angles are random in the game."
  - "Effective thickness spreads and stacks leave out glancing rays, counted in glancing_rays: a plate before or at the citadel is struck at or past the AP shell's always-ricochet angle and not overmatched, or, without an AP shell or on an overmatched plate, at 80 deg or more from its normal."
  - "Approaches fire at the model's starboard side with the hull level, no heel or pitch, and turrets at their default heading."
